ok     a block never filled misses
ok     a filled block hits with the bytes it was filled with
ok     the backend is part of the key
ok     each core has its own slots
ok     the least recently used block goes, not the one read every step
ok     the oldest data block was the one given up
ok     a write on another core retires this core's copies
ok     the core that wrote keeps what it wrote
ok     a failed write retires the block and keeps no copy
ok     a write around the cache retires every copy
ok     every hit is counted
